<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RSW_ZakkroEgg.xml                               EXTREME_DESERT_CAVERN_BEAST_1

  The egg half of this item, paired with RSW_Zakkro (DesertPort/RSW_Zakkro.xml
  — read that file's header first). deep_desert.md SS4 "Eggs are canteens":
  "A large egg is portable water in a rigid shell... It is not food, it is
  drink you can carry." This is NOT the mudhorn's already-shipped hatching/
  food egg pair (RSW_EggMudhornFertilized/Unfertilized, MLIE_FAUNA_ABSORPTION_1)
  — deliberately a single, non-hatching resource item:

  - Parented on vanilla EggUnfertBase (the same abstract every never-hatches
    unfertilized egg in this mod uses, e.g. RSW_EggMudhornUnFertilized) and
    carries NO CompProperties_Hatcher — there is no fertilized sibling and
    nothing here ever produces a Zakkro pawn. See RSW_Zakkro.xml's header for
    why the creature itself also carries no CompProperties_EggLayer.
  - No CompProperties_Rottable. deep_desert.md SS6 hard-bans rot/decay content
    in this biome outright ("nothing rots... any content assuming
    putrefaction... is a violation"), and narratively the sealed shell is
    exactly why the water inside keeps.
  - ingestible foodType Fluid + DesperateOnlyForHumanlikes preferability,
    matching FlowWorks' own bottled-water items
    (RM_LiquidBottles.xml:RM_Bottle_FreshWater) — "drunk for survival," not a
    tasty meal. Not wired into FlowWorks' RM_BottledLiquidExtension/bottle-fill
    job system: that framework is for refillable containers filled from
    terrain, and this is a found, single-use natural resource, not a bottle.
  - High Nutrition/Mass/MarketValue relative to a normal egg, since the whole
    point is that one of these is worth crossing a desert for.

  Not wired into any ThingSetMaker/loot table or cavern-generation content —
  that placement is cavern map-generation's job and out of scope for this item.

  Art: checked infrastructure/artpipe/{done,_artsrc,registry.jsonl,
  art_status.json} for "zakkro egg"/"cave beast egg" first — nothing existed.
  Job rsw_zakkroegg_v1 filed this pass; texPath below is where the render will
  land, pending until the artpipe daemon delivers.
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="EggUnfertBase">
    <defName>RSW_ZakkroEgg</defName>
    <label>zakkro egg</label>
    <description>A single massive egg out of a zakkro's cavern nest, its thick shell packed with cool reserve water rather than yolk — the reason a Jawa will cross open sand for one. Cracked open it drains like a canteen; there is no chick inside to lose, and nothing about it rots or spoils in the shell.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <!-- No existing render found (checked done/_artsrc/registry.jsonl/art_status.json,
           2026-09-20). Job rsw_zakkroegg_v1 filed. -->
      <texPath>swresource/RSW_ZakkroEgg</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_StackCount</graphicClass>
      <drawSize>1.8</drawSize>
      <color>(216,204,178)</color>
      <!-- bone/dust pale, per the biome's ban on anything reading mineralized or gemstone -->
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <MarketValue>320</MarketValue>
      <Mass>4.0</Mass>
      <Nutrition>2.5</Nutrition>
    </statBases>
    <ingestible>
      <foodType>Fluid</foodType>
      <preferability>DesperateOnlyForHumanlikes</preferability>
      <tasteThought>AteRawFood</tasteThought>
      <optimalityOffsetFeedingAnimals>-50</optimalityOffsetFeedingAnimals>
    </ingestible>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
